    "title": "<p>Endometriosis: distribution and prevalence</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Ayse Ayhan",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGridLight\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"0\" width=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 3.5pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 386.85pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" colspan=\"3\" width=\"516\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Location</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.2pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"176\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><strong>% of all endometriosis</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.25pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><strong>References</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 386.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"3\" width=\"516\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Pelvic (2&ndash;30% of women of reproductive age)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"176\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.85pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"18\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 373.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"497\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Ovary</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"176\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">17&ndash;65%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{31311360; 30240947}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"18\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 373.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"497\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Uterine ligaments (uterosacral &gt; broad &gt; inguinal)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"176\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">3&ndash;69%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{17102045; 30240947}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.85pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"18\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 373.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"497\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Fallopian tube</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"176\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">10&ndash;44%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{31517305}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"18\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 373.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"497\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Peritoneum superficial</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"176\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">6.4&ndash;15.2%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{24352888}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.85pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"18\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 373.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"497\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Pelvic nerves<sup>a</sup></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"176\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">More common than expected</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{20869701}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 386.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"3\" width=\"516\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>Extrapelvic<sup>b</sup><strong> (0.25&ndash;3.6% of women of reproductive age)</strong></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"176\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{27992931; 31427853; 29320327}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.85pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"18\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 373.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"497\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Abdominal</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"176\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"18\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"18\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 359.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"479\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Gastrointestinal tract (sigmoid &gt; rectum &gt; ileum &gt; appendix &gt; caecum)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"176\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">3.8&ndash;37%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{900194; 30363647}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.85pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"18\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.85pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"18\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 359.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"479\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Urinary tract (bladder &gt; ureter &gt; kidney &gt; urethra)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"176\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">0.3&ndash;12%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{30165449; 30363647; 30240947}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"18\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"18\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 359.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"479\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Diaphragm</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"176\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">0.7&ndash;1%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{11821085}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.85pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"18\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 373.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"497\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Thoracic (diaphragm &gt; pleura &gt; lungs &gt; pericardium)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"176\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">0.01&ndash;0.7%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{11821085}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"18\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 373.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"497\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Skin (including umbilical area)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"176\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">0.5&ndash;1%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{27992931}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.85pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"18\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 373.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"497\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">External genitalia (vagina &gt; perineum &gt; vulva)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"176\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">0.3&ndash;1.4%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{22422793}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.85pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"18\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 373.0pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"497\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Others (muscle, breast, brain, other)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.2pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"176\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Rare</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.25pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">&ndash;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>a</sup>Pelvic nerves include the sciatic, obturator, femoral, and pudendal nerves and the inferior hypogastric and lumbosacral plexuses.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>b</sup>Extrapelvic: ~12% of women with pelvic endometriosis have extrapelvic disease (e.g. in the liver, gallbladder, or pancreas); extrapelvic endometriosis is typically associated with pelvic disease.</p>",
